    "site_desc": "The field has been no-till, rainfed, and was planted with alfalfa in 2009-2013, see Saliendra et al 2018 https://doi.org/10.1002/ecs2.2147, corn in 2014, and sunflower in 2015. The LTAR Cropland Common Experiment started in 2016 with treatment for the site as \"Business-As-Usual (BAU) or Prevailing Practice (PP)\", i.e., no-till, rainfed, 3-year rotation of spring wheat-corn-soybean and management aligned with local farmers' practices, see Liebig et al 2022. https://doi.org/10.1002/agg2.20291",
